WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:01.166
(audience laughing)

00:00:01.166 --> 00:00:02.670
- I used to be a teacher you know that,

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:03.790
some of you, right?

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:05.020
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:06.462
Teachers here tonight?

00:00:06.462 --> 00:00:07.330
(audience cheering)

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:08.880
Bless you, you heroes.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:11.417
Look at this quote I found about you.

00:00:11.417 --> 00:00:13.793
"The best teachers are those
that tell you where to look

00:00:13.793 --> 00:00:16.347
"but they don't tell you what to see."

00:00:16.347 --> 00:00:17.840
(audience whooping)

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:18.673
It's true!

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:20.373
You know what?

00:00:20.373 --> 00:00:22.630
I taught for 13 years and
I thought I was great.

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:25.210
It's the only thing that's kept
me going cause I, honestly,

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:26.929
I fucking hate children.

00:00:26.929 --> 00:00:28.880
(audience laughing)

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:30.110
I thought I was good.

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:33.320
It's the only thing that I've
clung onto all these years.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:36.760
And the kids liked me and I
never did them a disservice.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:38.870
Anyway, I met some of them
in the same week (laughs)

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:40.010
as I saw Elsie.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:41.720
I met some of my ex-pupils.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:43.790
And I've got another quote
for you now, from one of them.

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:44.623
See what you make of this.

00:00:44.623 --> 00:00:45.630
It's a genuine quote.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:52.029
(audience laughing and cheering)

00:00:52.029 --> 00:00:55.029
(audience clapping)

00:00:56.143 --> 00:00:58.860
And when I stopped to really
think about it for ten seconds,

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:00.030
I was shit.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:03.594
I was a drama teacher, which
in itself is hilarious, right?

00:01:03.594 --> 00:01:04.561
(audience laughing)

00:01:04.561 --> 00:01:05.535
(short laugh)

00:01:05.535 --> 00:01:06.750
And you know when I knew
I had to give up teaching?

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.293
I was in my drama studio,

00:01:08.293 --> 00:01:10.610
and the kids were performing a play

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:13.020
that they'd been working on
for weeks, while I smoked

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:14.581
at the back of the drama studio.

00:01:14.581 --> 00:01:15.918
And, I'd finally run out of time

00:01:15.918 --> 00:01:17.610
and they had to perform them.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:21.890
And they were really
(laughs) excited and focused.

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:24.290
And I realized that someone
was up in the lighting tower

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:25.710
of the drama studio,

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:27.540
aggressively throwing Blu Tack

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:29.000
into their faces.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.050
While they were performing.

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:31.950
And I mean really like nastily!

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:33.427
Spitefully throwing it.

00:01:33.427 --> 00:01:34.977
And it was bouncing off
them and they were going,

00:01:34.977 --> 00:01:37.020
"Get off, get off, get off."

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:38.120
It was awful!

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:40.730
And I knew I had to give
up teaching when I realized

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:43.478
that the person up there
throwing that Blu Tack,

00:01:43.478 --> 00:01:44.311
(audience laughing)

00:01:44.311 --> 00:01:45.473
that's right, was me!

00:01:45.473 --> 00:01:46.556
(audience laughing)

00:01:46.556 --> 00:01:48.919
It was me and I was with
the Head of English.

00:01:48.919 --> 00:01:49.752
(audience laughing)

00:01:49.752 --> 00:01:52.459
And we were laughing our bollocks off.

00:01:52.459 --> 00:01:55.459
(audience laughing)

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:01.040
And it was at that point I realized,

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:05.050
my perception of how
I think people see me,

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:08.410
and other people's perception
are very different things.

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:11.800
And when you start to think
about it, it panics you.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:14.120
And the worst thing is, your perception,

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:17.513
or rather your reputation
can be ruined, like that!

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:19.940
I'm gonna show you three quotes now.

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:21.970
They're all from actual friends of mine.

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:25.680
And they're so insane they
changed my view of that person,

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:27.600
and I wrote it on my phone immediately.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:28.433
Right?

00:02:28.433 --> 00:02:31.690
The first one is from
a 37-year-old (laughs)

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:32.540
science teacher.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:34.490
She could be teaching your children.

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:36.460
I had a one-hour row with her in a pub,

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:39.983
because she said, and
she fucking meant this.

00:02:43.549 --> 00:02:46.549
(audience laughing)

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:51.734
She thinks you can stretch yourself.

00:02:51.734 --> 00:02:53.150
(audience laughing)

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:55.890
I went to an Urban Zoo with
a 40-year-old friend of mine,

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:57.370
who's a mother of two.

00:02:57.370 --> 00:02:59.920
She saw a turkey and she said this.

00:03:01.495 --> 00:03:04.553
(audience laughing)

00:03:04.553 --> 00:03:05.670
Happy Christmas!

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:08.391
He's just (mumbles) is
a massive male chicken!

00:03:08.391 --> 00:03:11.190
(audience laughing)

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:14.480
But by far the worst, a
52-year-old friend of mine,

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:17.010
who is a successful CEO of a company.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:20.390
I made reference to the
irritating buzzing wings of a fly,

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:22.290
that was in the room and he said this.

00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:26.667
(audience laughing)

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.145
He thinks flies are shouting!

00:03:29.145 --> 00:03:30.603
(audience laughing)

00:03:30.603 --> 00:03:31.436
Yeah!

00:03:32.533 --> 00:03:33.747
I'm a fly!

00:03:33.747 --> 00:03:34.964
(audience laughing)

00:03:34.964 --> 00:03:36.126
I'm flying!

00:03:36.126 --> 00:03:37.303
(audience laughing)

00:03:37.303 --> 00:03:39.580
Presumably when they stop and land

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:41.409
they're having a fucking breath are they?

00:03:41.409 --> 00:03:42.628
(audience laughing)

00:03:42.628 --> 00:03:45.828
(panting heavily)

00:03:45.828 --> 00:03:46.661
Yeah!

00:03:46.661 --> 00:03:47.523
Let's do this!

00:03:47.523 --> 00:03:48.980
Yeah, I'm flying.

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:51.560
(audience laughing)

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:54.040
Nothing that man can say

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:56.240
will alter my new perception of him,

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:58.672
that he is fundamentally,
thick as pig shit.

00:03:58.672 --> 00:04:02.755
(audience laughing and clapping)

